WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.496
I needed histological sections of zebrafish embryos.

00:00:03.496 --> 00:00:06.192
They were small, and their orientation mattered:

00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:08.887
a slice through the wrong plane could

00:00:08.887 --> 00:00:11.583
miss the anatomy I wanted to study.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.367
My first step used two percent agarose

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.933
as a support. I could position the

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:23.500
specimens before the paraffin step, with the

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.066
hope of preserving the chosen plane during

00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:26.433
sectioning.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.874
The proposal depended on two different materials.

00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:36.948
Agarose maintained orientation; paraffin was supposed to

00:00:36.948 --> 00:00:40.022
support thin sections after processing. The second

00:00:40.022 --> 00:00:43.096
stage would have to integrate with the

00:00:43.096 --> 00:00:43.535
first.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.269
This is the real processing apparatus from

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:50.738
that attempt. It records what was tried,

00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:53.206
but a photograph of the instrument is

00:00:53.206 --> 00:00:55.675
not evidence that a usable section was

00:00:55.675 --> 00:00:56.028
made.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.851
Instead of behaving like one mechanically coherent

00:01:03.851 --> 00:01:06.903
block, the embedded materials formed distinguishable layers.

00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:09.954
A sectioning method that works with one

00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:13.005
solid block may fail when the material

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:13.877
interface separates.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.519
Here is the actual block in the

00:01:18.519 --> 00:01:21.238
microtome. At sectioning the material separated and

00:01:21.238 --> 00:01:23.957
broke apart. The problem was no longer

00:01:23.957 --> 00:01:26.676
merely positioning a fish; it was obtaining

00:01:26.676 --> 00:01:27.841
a sectionable composite.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.666
I did not obtain reliable, interpretable histological

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:36.532
sections from this sequence. Nothing here is

00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:39.399
a successful stained slide, and these photographs

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.265
should not be used to imply one.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.938
The failure suggests questions for a new

00:01:48.938 --> 00:01:52.077
method: embedding compatibility, processing, and orientation controls.

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:55.215
Those are experiments still to perform, not

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.457
results I have already produced.
